00:00:01.060 --> 00:00:03.830
Rhiannon: If parents have a good
relationship with their child, they will

00:00:03.830 --> 00:00:07.930
usually find that the child is more likely
to open up to them about their problems.

00:00:08.559 --> 00:00:12.200
One of the most important ways
parents can help, is to listen to them

00:00:12.250 --> 00:00:13.870
and take their feelings seriously.

00:00:14.639 --> 00:00:17.740
Leah: Children and young people’s
negative feelings usually pass, but

00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:21.400
it’s a good idea to get help and
support if this goes on longer and

00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:24.430
their negative feelings are stopping
them from getting on with their lives.

00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:29.220
Rhiannon: Especially if their distress
is disrupting family life or if they

00:00:29.220 --> 00:00:33.130
are repeatedly behaving in ways that
would not be expected at their age.

00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:37.810
Leah: If a child or young person is having
problems at school, a teacher, school

00:00:37.810 --> 00:00:41.879
nurse, school counsellor or educational
psychologist may be able to help.

00:00:42.390 --> 00:00:45.060
Otherwise parents or
carers can approach a GP.

00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:49.040
Professionals are able to refer a
child to further help such as Child and

00:00:49.049 --> 00:00:51.290
Adolescent Mental Health Services [CAMHS].

00:00:51.880 --> 00:00:55.900
Most support is provided free by
the NHS, the school or a local

00:00:55.920 --> 00:00:57.870
council’s social services department.

00:00:58.450 --> 00:01:01.990
Rhiannon: Treatments for children and
young people with mental health problems

00:01:02.330 --> 00:01:06.899
put a lot of emphasis on talking and
on understanding the problem in order

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:08.799
to work out the best way to tackle it.

00:01:09.270 --> 00:01:11.650
For younger children, this
may be done through play.

00:01:12.760 --> 00:01:16.190
Leah: Children and young people always
need to be assessed by a specialist

00:01:16.410 --> 00:01:18.570
before they are prescribed any medication.

00:01:19.410 --> 00:01:22.649
Children and young people can seek
help on their own, if they wish, by

00:01:22.650 --> 00:01:26.840
ringing a helpline or approaching a
professional directly, but consent

00:01:26.860 --> 00:01:30.130
is usually needed for them to get
medical care if they are under 16.

00:01:31.340 --> 00:01:33.990
Rhiannon: Early intervention can
help with children's social and

00:01:33.990 --> 00:01:38.100
emotional development including
increasing their social interaction and

00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:42.389
behaviour, improving self-esteem and
reducing the incidents of clinically

00:01:42.389 --> 00:01:44.300
diagnosed mental health problems.

00:01:45.490 --> 00:01:52.210
Leah: Let’s hear from a professional
about how early intervention can help.

